`addSignatures` drops the store's cached path info for the path.

`LocalStore::addSignatures` writes the new signatures to SQLite, and
`RemoteStore::addSignatures` sends them to the daemon. Neither touches
`pathInfoCache`, so a later `queryPathInfo` on the same Store answers
the signatures the path had before. The nix CLI does not see it: each
command is a new process with an empty cache. A huggorm Store lives for
the session, and `add_signatures` then `query_path_info` answered no
signatures (measured on 2.35.2, tests/test_signature.py).

`BinaryCacheStore` writes a new .narinfo and upserts the cache, so it
needs no change.

Reported as Lillecarl/nix#425. It is meant for upstream.

--- a/src/libstore/local-store.cc
+++ b/src/libstore/local-store.cc
@@ -1577,8 +1577,10 @@
         updatePathInfo(*state, *info);

         txn.commit();
     });
+
+    invalidatePathInfoCacheFor(storePath);
 }

